-- NEGATIVE fixture for the rule-date interval table (spec §15.3, R10).
--
-- A law-time-guarded OBLIGATION. This is the shape temporal rule-versioning
-- most invites -- "under the 2024 rules the issuer must file within 30 days,
-- before that within 45" -- and it is exactly the shape DMN cannot model at
-- all: a deontic body is a transition system, not a value, and DMN "has no
-- notion of time" and cannot hold an obligation as a state.
--
-- `rowsToDmnWith'` refuses it with `RegulativeBody` BEFORE it builds anything,
-- but the dated path does not go through `rowsToDmnWith'`. So `datedChain`
-- restates that refusal by answering `NotDated`, which routes the decision back
-- to the ordinary path and to its existing `RegulativeBody` fallback.
--
-- Expected: NO D-DATEDCHAIN, no decision table, and a D-LITERALEXPR whose
-- reason is the deontic body -- not `D-NONFEELOUTPUT`, which would be a
-- statement about RENDERING standing in for the categorical fact that DMN
-- cannot hold an obligation.
--
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`. Asserted from jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `law-time guarded obligation`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Issuer

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `file the annual report`

GIVETH A DATE
`the 2024 amendment` MEANS Date 1 1 2024

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`filing duty` MEANS
    IF   `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST `the 2024 amendment`
    THEN PARTY Issuer MUST `file the annual report` WITHIN 30
    ELSE PARTY Issuer MUST `file the annual report` WITHIN 45
